{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pulls/117","id":5106607681,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUSUYw88AAAABMGCmQQ","html_url":"https://github.com/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pull/117","diff_url":"https://github.com/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pull/117.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pull/117.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/issues/117","number":117,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(reg06): admit Operator Drop as a product capability and implement durable PIT market-data persistence","user":{"login":"ramkivs","id":302525469,"node_id":"U_kgDOEggsHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/302525469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs","html_url":"https://github.com/ramkivs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Authority\n\nExpress PA (Ramki) authorization of **2026-11-01** for full one-pass execution. This is the **\"Express `REG-06` promotion/admission act\"** that the `P-08` pending-register row named as the required decision, and the **\"approved manual-ingestion product requirement\"** whose absence the 2026-10-13 register entry and `GOV-REC-2026-NON-PROD-OPERATOR-BYPASS-01` cited as the reason for deferral.\n\nGovernance record `IIPS_V3_REG06_OPERATOR_DROP_PRODUCT_ADMISSION_2026-11-01` / `CHG-2026-11-01-01` appended to the IPD execution tracker as a **dated superseding overlay**. The 2026-10-13 `DEFERRED` disposition and the `P-08` records are **retained verbatim** — dated overlays govern historical text.\n\n## What was already reusable (not reimplemented)\n\n- **Series-qualified ISIN resolution** — `buildD114SecurityIdentity` / `isD114SecurityIdentity` / `PitReadService`, already implemented, exported via `./pit` and tested on `main`.\n- `OperatorDropParser` — reused unchanged via a recording pipeline wrapper (zero parser edits).\n- `IngestionPipeline` canonicalization and DLQ quarantine; `migration_ledger.ts` transactional ledger.\n\n## What was implemented\n\n| Capability | Location |\n|---|---|\n| Durable PIT market-data persistence | `src/pit/pit_durable_store.ts` — `DurablePointInTimeStore<T>`, `UNIQUE (pit_key, as_of_ms)`, own migration ledger |\n| Operator Drop → series identity → durable writes | `src/operator_drop/drop_ingestion.ts` |\n| Product runtime caller (ingest → screen) | `src/operator_drop/product_runtime.ts` |\n| Package-export admission | `./operator-drop` export map + `src/operator_drop/package.ts` |\n\n**Migration isolation:** `GATE3_MIGRATIONS` and `DESIGNATED_MIGRATION_BLOBS` are untouched — check `V-A2-1` requires exactly four rows, so the Gate A′ / P-1 chain is undisturbed. The durable store uses its own database file and its own ledger.\n\n**Identity is required, never inferred.** A record with no explicit `securityIdentity` (or explicit `isin` + `series`) is rejected with a named reason and never silently admitted under `companyId`. No cross-series fallback.\n\n## Design finding worth flagging\n\n`IngestionPipeline` stamps every envelope with **time-derived** identity (`envelopeId` as `env-<epoch>-<nonce>`, `provenance.evaluatedAt`, `provenance.dataVersion` and therefore `provenance.lineageHash`). Digesting the whole envelope therefore **can never report a duplicate** — a byte-identical replay is misclassified as a conflicting snapshot. `computeSnapshotDigest` keys on the admitted data `[pitKey, asOf, payload]`, so a replay is idempotent while genuinely different market data at the same identity and instant still fails closed as `SNAPSHOT_CONFLICT`.\n\n## Reconciliation of earlier findings\n\n1. **Series-qualified ISIN resolution already existed on `main`** — the `P-08` row listed it as an unmet prerequisite. What was genuinely absent was the **wiring from Operator Drop to it** (`src/operator_drop/**` held zero ISIN references).\n2. **Durable PIT market-data persistence did not exist** and was correctly identified as absent. NP-04's `GovernedArtifactStore` persists governed *report* artifacts and is unmerged.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run build` | success |\n| `npm test` | **987 tests / 986 passed / 0 failed / 1 skipped** (baseline 941 / 940 / 0) |\n| `npm run test:package-consumer` | **PASS** — 6 PASS, 0 FAIL, `verbatimCopies: true`, `productionModuleRuntime: PASS`, **`browser.forbiddenHits: []`** |\n\n46 new tests cover all eight required categories: durable writes + restart recovery; duplicate ingestion / idempotency; invalid or ambiguous identity rejection; same ISIN across series with no cross-series fallback; historical-date correctness and PIT retrieval; persistence failure / partial-write recovery; package exports and public API compatibility; actual product runtime caller + end-to-end ingestion-to-screening.\n\nThree pre-existing **exact-contract** assertions were updated to the newly authorized surface (`./pit` 2 → 6 symbols; export map 3 → 4 subpaths in two files). **None was weakened, deleted or skipped** — each still pins its contract exactly.\n\n## Boundaries preserved\n\n- **IRR: read-only.** No IRR file created, modified or pushed. IRR-side reconciliation is a **separate IRR work item** and is **not** established by this change.\n- **Production: out of scope.** No deployment, activation, provisioning or host execution.\n- Unchanged: `GATE3_MIGRATIONS`, `DESIGNATED_MIGRATION_BLOBS`, check `V-A2-1`, the Gate A′ / P-1 chain, write guards, dispatch's closed write-operation set, authorization guards, production eligibility.\n- `O-05` remains **OPEN**. `P-1-C` **NOT ESTABLISHED**. `P-1-D` **DESIGNATED, NOT VERIFIED FOR THE ATTEMPT**. `P-1` authorized by IRR P1-F (2026-10-29) — **ONE ATTEMPT ONLY — NOT EXECUTED — UNSPENT**.\n\nThis is not production admission, not `AD-17 / M-2` authorization, and confers no IRR acceptance.","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:47:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:22Z","closed_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:22Z","merged_at":"2026-11-01T10:48:22Z","merge_commit_sha":"eb9289222e2bdfd0e79381d4d81f7f81715e019b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pulls/117/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pulls/117/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/issues/117/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramkivs/iips-production-market-data/statuses/5b2c03dc8888aa40a4dd967ef6e7f3b76731c01e","head":{"label":"ramkivs:arena/442f31c6-iips-production-market-data","ref":"arena/442f31c6-iips-production-market-data","sha":"5b2c03dc8888aa40a4dd967ef6e7f3b76731c01e","user":{"login":"ramkivs","id":302525469,"node_id":"U_kgDOEggsHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/302525469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs","html_url":"https://github.com/ramkivs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramkivs/following{/other_user}","gi